course: dictionary
lesson: 8711
title: Sensation: feelings and excitement
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A sensation is a feeling. Some sensations come from your body, like a burning sensation or a tingling sensation in your hand. Other sensations are harder to name, like a strange feeling that someone is watching you.
explain: Look at the clues in «In the middle of the trial Alice feels a curious sensation: she is growing again.» The words after the colon tell you what the sensation is: she is growing. So a sensation here is a strange feeling that is hard to describe. Curious means strange or unusual.
explain: Sensation can also mean great excitement, as in «The new singer is a sensation.» Here the sensation is the singer, a person who causes a lot of excitement. A good check is to swap in another word: "feeling" fits the first sentence, but it does not fit the singer sentence, so you know the meaning has changed.
fact: Sensation means a feeling, often one that you notice through your body or your senses.
fact: «A burning sensation» means a feeling of heat or stinging.
fact: «Loss of sensation in the fingers» means you cannot feel anything there. If this happens after an injury, get help.
fact: «A strange sensation of being watched» is a general feeling that is hard to explain.
fact: «The new singer is a sensation» means the singer is a big hit who causes great excitement.
exercise: «In the middle of the trial Alice feels a curious sensation: she is growing again.» What does sensation mean here? | *A strange feeling in the body | A cold, wet day | A loud noise | A group of people cheering
exercise: «The new singer is a sensation.» What does sensation mean here? | A burning feeling | A quiet, gloomy mood | A feeling in the fingers | *Someone causing great excitement
exercise: Ella says her fingers have lost sensation after the cold. What does this mean? | *She cannot feel her fingers properly | Her fingers are very warm and happy | She has a new ring | Her fingers are growing longer
test: «He felt a strange sensation of being watched.» What does sensation mean? | A sweet taste | A loud shout | A sensible plan | *A general feeling that is hard to explain
test: In «a tingling sensation», which word could replace sensation? | castle | silence | *feeling | sunshine
exam: Jayden says a sensation can only be a feeling in the body. Is he right? | No, it means a loud noise | Yes, it is always a body feeling | *No, it can also be a general feeling, or great excitement caused by a person or thing | Yes, but only in science
